# apps/web/app/seo/lastmod.generated.json is generated by
# apps/web/scripts/generate-seo-lastmod.mjs and committed so that a build with
# no git history (Vercel's shallow clone) still has stable sitemap timestamps.
#
# `-merge` because a conflict here is never informative. The generator stamps
# one timestamp onto every route whose content digest changed, so two branches
# editing the same docs page always overlap, and the right resolution is always
# to regenerate rather than to pick a side. Without this, git writes conflict
# markers into the JSON, which leaves it unparseable — so the generator cannot
# run and the marker-ridden generated file has to be hand-edited first.
#
# With it, git still reports the conflict, but leaves valid JSON in the
# worktree. Resolve with:
#
#     pnpm --dir apps/web seo:lastmod && git add apps/web/app/seo/lastmod.generated.json
#
# Chosen over a custom merge driver, which every clone would have to register
# in its own git config before it took effect.
apps/web/app/seo/lastmod.generated.json -merge linguist-generated=true
